   "key": "§ Emuqu > Privacy",
   "hash": "cb9b3ea1342e3ee8",
   "does": "No server/accounts; iCloud sync off until enabled; table of third-party egress: CloudKit (encrypted, no HealthKit data), hosted AI (with consent; on every turn the live-state block from AssistantContext.renderLiveStateForCloud; DeepSeek PRC disclosure in ProviderConsentSheet), Apple Intelligence row: Quick sends nothing beyond web search/map lookups; with a consented Grok or DeepSeek, Auto sends classifier-flagged turns and Deep every turn to it (TierProviderMapper.autoMapping/deepMapping, reached only while Apple is the selected provider) with the same data a hosted turn carries; in every tier mode voice turns and email/directions/web-search requests go to the first consented hosted provider (TurnRouter voice bypass and action-intent override). Then Apple speech, Tavily/Anthropic web search, MET Norway at ~1 km (WeatherService rounds to 2 decimals), Overpass, Apple geocoder, OpenTopoData ~11 m, Hugging Face for the WhisperKit model. The closing paragraph says Quick/Auto/Deep apply only with Apple selected and that Auto and Deep can send a turn to a consented Grok or DeepSeek. API keys in Keychain ThisDeviceOnly, never synced (APIKeyStore). Overpass requests carry a User-Agent with the author's email (OverpassClient) — identifies the app to the operator, not data sent to the author.",
